# RTL timing / CDC (710)

Thin always-on when editing constraints or FPGA timing scripts. CDC depth in `sc-rtl` `references/intent-cdc.md`. Timing gate: `sc-rtl-verify` L5.

## Clocks

- Declare every primary clock; set period from SPEC / board (e.g. 50 MHz → 20 ns)
- Generated clocks (MMCM/PLL): define with correct multiply/divide; do not leave inferred-only
- Related synchronous clocks: keep timed unless SPEC says otherwise

## CDC (async domains)

- Structural sync: ≥2 FF chain on single-bit async signals; mark sync flops (`ASYNC_REG` / vendor keep) so they are not optimized away
- Do **not** use bare 2FF sync for multi-bit data or handshake protocols - use gray FIFO / valid-ready with proper sync
- Constraints: `set_clock_groups -asynchronous` **or** scoped `set_false_path` / `set_max_delay -datapath_only` for controlled latency - pick one policy and document
- Never leave async CDC paths fully timed without exception (false slack kills closure)

## Reset

- Sync deassert into each clock domain at system boundary (reset controller), not buried inside reusable IP
- Do not gate free-running reset with random datapath logic

## Closure evidence

- After PnR: timing report must meet target Fmax (or document miss + plan)
- Resource / LUT headroom: check against target report - fail closed if over budget without waiver
- Open flow (Yosys/nextpnr): treat nextpnr timing / `icetime` (or project report) as evidence via `spacecraft evidence`
